## Context

Reuse the pilot to reconcile Indonesian official plan/progress inventories and country observations without conflating approval, commitment and payment.

Design: `docs/jetp-backend-design.md`, revision 5. Plan: `docs/jetp-backend-implementation-plan.md`. Parent: 0760 (except the tracker itself, which belongs to 0725/#1333). Proposed work; no implementation authorized by filing.

## First test

The same programme appears in a plan and later approval inventory with a component and no payment evidence. Preserve both positions and scopes; no disbursement or additive double count may be generated.

## Actions

Pin official editions; enumerate inventories and IDN portfolio observation rows; classify/crosswalk all legacy inputs with explicit source locations, date roles, amounts and perimeter decisions. Retain useful editorial evidence and unresolved identities. Produce candidate differences and writer-transfer report.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All official inventory and IDN legacy rows have reviewed dispositions
- [ ] Plan/approval/payment meanings and component relations remain distinct
- [ ] Existing routes and source links remain viable
- [ ] Unexplained candidate differences block transfer

## Validation and recovery

Start implementation with the failing fixture. Run make check-fast and make lint; run the full make check for pipeline-surface diffs under AGENTS.md. Run the existing browser exercise for output/renderer changes. Cite exact fixture IDs and input/output commits in the PR. Preserve last accepted static output; candidate failure must not change canonical ownership or publish partial files. No deployment, estimator or PyPSA work is included in this ticket.

